cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Nanopore3"
abstract: >-
  A portable, reproducible pipeline for demultiplexing Oxford Nanopore amplicon
  reads by plate and well barcode, assigning them to designed references,
  building per-clone consensus sequences, and reporting quality-control evidence.
  Supports whole-vector references, and recovery of the source culture plate when
  several were pooled into one colony-PCR plate.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fryer
    given-names: Thomas
    email: tjaf@mit.edu
    affiliation: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0
keywords:
  - nanopore
  - amplicon sequencing
  - consensus
  - demultiplexing
  - protein design
  - plasmid sequencing
